[38;5;252m[1m## Translation Bugs Found & Fixed in [38;5;10msrc/polynomial.rs[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C code uses [38;5;10mint64_t % uint64_t[0m in several polynomial functions. In C, this implicitly converts the [38;5;10mint64_t[0m to [38;5;10muint64_t[0m before the modulo operation, so [38;5;10m-3 % 10[0m becomes [38;5;10m18446744073709551613 % 10 = 3[0m. The Rust translation was using [38;5;10mvalue % modulus as i64[0m, which keeps signed semantics ([38;5;10m-3 % 10 = -3[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fixed 6 functions by changing the modulo pattern from [38;5;10m(a op b) % modulus as i64[0m to [38;5;10m((a op b) as u64 % modulus) as i64[0m:[0m[0m
- [38;5;10madd()[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msub()[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mmul()[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mfit()[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msub_scaler()[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10madd_scaler()[0m[0m[0m
